{"judgments": [
 {"clause_id": "c001", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The execution/Effective Date is left blank (\"July ¥, 2005\"), so the date from which the Employment Term, the third-anniversary termination date and the Restricted Period run cannot be fixed from the instrument. Every duration in the Agreement depends on that missing date.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.22}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c002", "issues": []},
 {"clause_id": "c003", "issues": [
   {"issue": "\"Board\" is defined as the Board of Directors of Ajuba only, yet Section 2.1 has the Employee report \"directly to the Board (or selected designee of the Board of Directors of the Parent)\" and Schedule 2.1 has him report to the Chairman, so the body actually entitled to direct and terminate him is unclear. The defined term does not square with those reporting provisions.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.12}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c004", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The definition is open-ended on both ends — \"such other entities serviced by the Company at any time\" and a catch-all \"and other related services\" appended to a long enumerated list — so the outer boundary of the restricted \"Business\" is indeterminate (ejusdem generis / expressio unius). Because Business is measured \"at any time during the Employment Term,\" its content also shifts with whatever the Company happened to do.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.44},
   {"issue": "This definition of \"Business\" is materially broader than the definition of \"Business\" in Section 1.A of the contemporaneous Noncompetition Agreement, which is limited to listed services \"for hospitals and physicians in the United States.\" Two agreements of even date thus impose non-competes measured by different definitions of the same term.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.30}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c005", "issues": [
   {"issue": "\"Code\" is defined but the Internal Revenue Code is never invoked anywhere in the operative text (Section 9.6 speaks only of withholding \"as required by law\"), leaving the definition without work to do. A reader must decide whether any tax-qualification concept was meant to be imported.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.06}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c006", "issues": [
   {"issue": "\"Company Technology\" reaches anything \"known to the Employee as a consequence of or through the Employee's employment,\" which does not distinguish items he created from general knowledge or skill he acquired, and has no time boundary. The scope of what must be assigned and never used again turns on that undefined phrase.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.22}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c007", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The definition sweeps in \"all information, in whatever form, regarding Parent, the Company their Business and their clients\" without any exclusion for publicly available or independently known information, and the missing punctuation after \"the Company\" obscures whose Business is meant. The illustrative list beginning \"including, without limitation\" does nothing to bound it.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.26}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c008", "issues": [
   {"issue": "Clause (b)(ii)'s test — first-year revenue exceeding \"the sum of (A) one percent (1%) of Ajuba's actual consolidated gross revenue ... and (B) the scheduled first-year gross revenue for such new contract\" — is circular, since the quantity measured is added to the threshold it must exceed. As drafted the condition can never be satisfied.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.35}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c009", "issues": [
   {"issue": "\"Customer\" is keyed to \"the date of termination of this Agreement,\" a date the Agreement never defines (termination of employment, expiry of the Employment Term, and termination of the Agreement are different events). It also extends to mere prospects \"actively sought,\" an undefined measure of contact.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.24}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c010", "issues": [
   {"issue": "Disputes over EBITDA are committed to \"the independent accountants regularly employed by Ajuba,\" the paying party's own auditors, with no standard, procedure or statement that their determination is final and binding. The provision also shifts between \"any fiscal year\" and the defined \"Fiscal Year.\"", "type": 1, "prob": 0.16}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c011", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The Employment Term ends on \"the third anniversary of this Agreement,\" while Section 8.1 fixes termination at \"the third anniversary of the Effective Date\" — two measuring dates that need not coincide given the undated signature block. Because the Restricted Period in Section 1.14 runs three years from the end of the Employment Term, the discrepancy propagates.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.24}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c012", "issues": [
   {"issue": "\"or such other 12-month period as may constitute Ajuba's fiscal year at any time hereafter\" lets one party unilaterally redefine the measuring period on which the Bonus tables in Section 2.2(b) depend. No notice or limit is attached.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.09}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c013", "issues": []},
 {"clause_id": "c014", "issues": []},
 {"clause_id": "c015", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The \"Restricted Area\" here includes India, whereas Section 1.E of the contemporaneous Noncompetition Agreement defines the Restricted Area as \"the United States, its territories and protectorates\" only. The two instruments executed the same day therefore describe different geographic reach for materially identical covenants.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.30}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c016", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The Restricted Period ends \"three years after the end of the Employment Term,\" but the Employment Term itself may end early under Article VIII or run to the third anniversary, and nothing addresses employment continuing past that anniversary — so the covenant's end date cannot be computed. The total restraint may run anywhere from three to six years.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.42},
   {"issue": "This Restricted Period conflicts with Section 1.D of the contemporaneous Noncompetition Agreement, which runs three years from the date of that agreement, so the same conduct is restrained for two different periods. Section 9.8 preserves both instruments without reconciling them.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.32}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c017", "issues": [
   {"issue": "Section 2.1 requires the Employee to \"report directly to the Board (or selected designee of the Board of Directors of the Parent),\" while Schedule 2.1 — which the same section makes controlling — says he \"Reports to the Chairman of the Board of Ajuba International, Inc.\" The reporting line, which Section 8.4(a) makes relevant to Good Reason, cannot be read consistently.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.26},
   {"issue": "The duties are \"the duties as are customarily performed by a President\" plus \"such other legally permissible and proper duties\" consistent with his \"position,\" none of which is bounded, and \"full professional and business-related time\" is not defined. Whether a change in assignment breaches this section governs the Good Reason analysis.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.22}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c018", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The escalator says the Base Salary increases \"retroactive to the first business day of the year following the Fiscal Year in which such EBITDA was achieved,\" which is prospective rather than retroactive and leaves unclear whether the raise is permanent or repeats. It also does not say which Fiscal Year's EBITDA counts if the $3.5 million threshold is met more than once.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.30}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c019", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The Bonus tables state discrete EBITDA points with no rule for EBITDA falling between the tiers or above the top tier, and the lead-in says only that the Employee is \"eligible to receive\" a bonus rather than entitled to one. Whether the Bonus is discretionary or formulaic is left open.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.34}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c020", "issues": [
   {"issue": "This subsection entitles the Employee to participate in all benefit plans available to senior executives or employees generally, while Section 2.2(a) gives him the $18,800 Allowance expressly \"in lieu of receiving health, dental and other benefits afforded to Ajuba US employees.\" The two cannot both be given full effect.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.28}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c021", "issues": [
   {"issue": "\"Substantially similar to the D&O Policy maintained by the Company immediately prior to the date hereof\" fixes no limits, retention or coverage terms and depends on an unattached prior policy. Whether a replacement policy complies is unmeasurable from the text.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.16}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c022", "issues": [
   {"issue": "The commission is a percentage of \"net sales,\" and terminates twelve months after the contract \"goes live\" — neither term is defined anywhere in the Agreement. \"Samii,\" whose contracts trigger the 3% rate, is likewise never identified.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.30}
 ]},
 {"clause_id": "c023", "issues": [
